# Copy to .env and paste a real key. .env is gitignored — keep it that way.
#
# Two uses, both local-only:
#   1. Prefills the API key field during `npm run dev`, so you are not retyping
#      a key on every fresh browser profile. Never auto-verified.
#   2. Enables the opt-in smoke suite (`npm run test:smoke`), which transcribes
#      test-data/ against the real enclave.
#
# Get a key: https://portal.privatemode.ai
PRIVATEMODE_AI_API_KEY=

# ── Why this cannot leak ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vite exposes it as VITE_PRIVATEMODE_AI_API_KEY, read only behind
# `import.meta.env.DEV`. Production builds substitute DEV with false and
# eliminate the branch, so no key reaches dist/. CI additionally greps dist/ for
# key-shaped strings and fails the build on a hit — a bundle published to
# GitHub Pages is public to everyone. See ARCHITECTURE.md §8.2.
